         "1. Contact requirement: place the graduated edge of the scale flush against the object's surface to eliminate gap-induced angular deviations.\n2. Parallel alignment: ensure the ruler does not skew diagonally; if tilted at angle theta, the measured length L' = L / cos(theta) > L, introducing positive systematic error.\n3. Baseline alignment: align the 0.0 cm mark (or reference mark) precisely with the beginning edge of the block.\n4. Stability: hold both object and scale firmly to prevent slipping during reading.\n5. Terminal reading: observe the graduation mark touching the opposite terminating boundary.",
