         "1. Single pendulum (Linear simplicity): has 1 degree of freedom; restoring force is simple harmonic; predictable for centuries.\n2. Double pendulum (Coupled non-linearity):\n   - A second rod and bob are hinged directly to the tip of the first bob.\n   - Motion of the top bob alters the pivot position and gravitational potential of the lower bob.\n   - Motion of the lower bob jerks and exerts reactive torque on the upper bob.\n3. Extreme sensitivity to initial conditions (The Butterfly Effect):\n   - Release two double pendulums from positions differing by only 0.0001 millimetres.\n   - For the first 3 seconds: they swing nearly together.\n   - After 5 seconds: their paths diverge completely; one flips over in a loop while the other reverses direction!\n4. Distinction between random and chaotic: it is NOT random (it has no dice or chance—every motion obeys Newton's exact laws); but it is chaotic (infinitely sensitive and impossible to predict long-term).\n5. Weather forecasting parallel: explains why meteorologists cannot predict exact weather beyond 10-14 days.",
